{
 "_doc": [
  "CITY spec measurement regions (P1 City, round 07). ONE source of truth for builder and critic: run tools/export/city_spec_check.py <round_dir>.",
  "Boxes are [x0,y0,x1,y1] pixels. '1080' boxes refer to 1920x1080 frames, '4k' boxes to 3840x2160 frames (exactly 2x).",
  "Measurement rule (CITY-SPEC header): texture statistics (mean |Laplacian|, RMS contrast, flat 8x8 blocks) are taken on a 1920x1080 frame; a 4K frame is downscaled with INTER_AREA first.",
  "Mean-type statistics (Y, B-R, share of pixels above 204, percentiles) use the native frame with the box of that resolution. Y = .2126 R + .7152 G + .0722 B on the 8-bit sRGB frame.",
  "Facade boxes are hand-placed inside facade-only areas of the current S-view cameras (no sky, no street); if a camera changes they must be re-placed and the file version bumped.",
  "S4 far-field boxes: sky = top band left of the right-hand tower; far_shore = the skyline across the river only (no near-city pixels); river = open water right of the slab, left of the piers; near = the near roof (bottom-left).",
  "Round 06 disagreement (builder far_shore 0-900 x 215-300 / river 450-1250 x 330-400 vs critic far_shore 420-1400 x 180-235 / river 450-1000 x 260-330): the builder boxes contained near-city and pier pixels; these boxes replace both.",
  "Version 2 (round 09): the r08 street trees (S1 west sidewalk, S6 right foreground) grew over four v1 boxes, so their C1 / C2 numbers measured foliage, not facades (green-dominant share 36 % / 82 % / 30 % / 67 %). Re-placed to foliage-free wall (green share <= 1 %): s1_left_stone (0,0,190,235), s1_right_brick (1075,0,1335,230), s1_right_dark (1360,0,1690,290), s6_left_brown (0,20,270,180). Dropped, no foliage-free wall left in frame: s1_left_glass (fully behind a crown), s6_right_white. 16 daylight boxes + 3 dusk boxes remain (was 18 + 3). The v1 file is spec_regions_v1.json (r07 / r08 numbers).",
  "v3 (r10): crit_boxes = the r09 critic boxes, share of pixels above Y 204 <= max_pct204 (C1 1.5 %; S4 far band 10 %); S4 also gets T1 silhouette-top std >= 12 px from s4_far_check.silhouette_tops."
 ],
